NP-HALL-CHEM-AIR HA-O-ION-01 (NOMINAL member of the unweighted BEB / Thompson pair, OQ-HA-02). e + O(3P) -> O(+) + 2e. Byte-identical copy of docs/chemistry/o_o2/v0/tables/ionization_O_beb_kd2002.dat (sha256 1e3a377ede12d2fb20a9f4384c001b04e0d4ec260c4723cea5e1e261103e134e; v0 DRAFT, immutable), built by docs/chemistry/o_o2/v0/build_tables_nist107_o.py with abep_sim/rate_tables.py. Cross section: Kim & Desclaux, Phys. Rev. A 66, 012708 (2002), BEB direct + excitation-autoionization total, O(3P), via NIST SRD 107 (https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/Ionization/merge.php?file=OI--&mode=ASCII, raw sha256 76df7f7a223a803ab5902eeae0b557ffb2d3317ba692a37676851781a1d225d8, not committed: the same route and model as the in-use ionization_N.dat); 129 energies 13.62-5000 eV; sigma(13.618 eV) = 0 prepended; held above 5000 eV. Header 13.618 eV = O ionization energy (Itikawa & Ichimura, JPCRD 19, 637 (1990) Table 2.1; NIST SRD 107 atom page 13.6181 eV). No uncertainty stated in the NIST table; SONG2026: recommended O data accurate to at least 20 % where they matter; Thompson / BEB 0.868-1.064 over 20-200 eV (v0 manifest). Energy column = mean electron energy 3/2 Te. Evidence level 4 (docs/EVIDENCE.md); quantity type: model-derived. Rebuild needs the NIST raw file (host blocked here); the copy is checked against the v0 sha256 by abep_chem::hall_air.
